{"version":"6.9","hitCount":1,"request":{"queryString":"EXT_ID:42826334 AND SRC:MED","internalQuery":"EXT_ID:42826334 AND SRC:MED","resultType":"CORE","cursorMark":"*","pageSize":25,"sort":"","synonym":false},"resultList":{"result":[{"id":"42826334","source":"MED","pmid":"42826334","pmcid":"PMC13632975","fullTextIdList":{"fullTextId":["PMC13632975"]},"doi":"10.1097/md.0000000000050807","title":"Association of CYP2C19 genetic polymorphisms with dyslipidemia and ischemic cerebrovascular disease in the mongolian population: A case-control study.","authorString":"Hu G, Zhang J, Shi R, Yu J, Wang S, Hu B, Bao P, Wang Y.","authorList":{"author":[{"fullName":"Hu G","lastName":"Hu","firstName":"Gejile","initials":"G","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0009-9386-971"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurology, Tongliao People's Hospital, Tongliao, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Zhang J","lastName":"Zhang","firstName":"Jianhui","initials":"J","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0000-9050-7849"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurology, Tongliao People's Hospital, Tongliao, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Shi R","lastName":"Shi","firstName":"Rui","initials":"R","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0007-1662-3746"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurology, Tongliao People's Hospital, Tongliao, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Yu J","lastName":"Yu","firstName":"Jingyang","initials":"J","authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurology, Tongliao People's Hospital, Tongliao, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang S","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Shiyang","initials":"S","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0009-9202-6307"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurology, Tongliao People's Hospital, Tongliao, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Hu B","lastName":"Hu","firstName":"Baoqiang","initials":"B","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0000-2536-5346"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurology, Tongliao People's Hospital, Tongliao, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Bao P","lastName":"Bao","firstName":"Pengnan","initials":"P","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0008-6255-358"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurology, Tongliao People's Hospital, Tongliao, China."}]}},{"fullName":"Wang Y","lastName":"Wang","firstName":"Yue","initials":"Y","authorId":{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0003-6500-3448"},"authorAffiliationDetailsList":{"authorAffiliation":[{"affiliation":"Department of Neurology, Baotou Central Hospital, Baotou, China."}]}}]},"authorIdList":{"authorId":[{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0008-6255-358"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0009-9386-971"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0000-2536-5346"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0000-9050-7849"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0003-6500-3448"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0007-1662-3746"},{"type":"ORCID","value":"0009-0009-9202-6307"}]},"dataLinksTagsList":{"dataLinkstag":["supporting_data"]},"journalInfo":{"issue":"40","volume":"105","journalIssueId":4276935,"dateOfPublication":"2026 Oct","monthOfPublication":10,"yearOfPublication":2026,"journal":{"medlineAbbreviation":"Medicine (Baltimore)","title":"Medicine","essn":"1536-5964","issn":"0304-5412","nlmid":"2985248R","isoabbreviation":"Medicine (Baltimore)"},"printPublicationDate":"2026-10-01"},"pubYear":"2026","pageInfo":"e50807","abstractText":"This study investigates the role of cytochrome P450 2C19 (CYP2C19) gene polymorphisms and dyslipidaemic metabolism in ischemic cerebrovascular disease among Mongolian patients, analyzing their interaction with conventional risk factors. This case-control study enrolled 300 patients with ischemic cerebrovascular disease: 150 Mongolian patients (observation group) receiving CYP2C19 genotype-guided treatment and 150 Han Chinese patients (control group) undergoing standard care. Baseline characteristics, lipid profiles, CYP2C19 genotypes, NIHSS, and activities of daily living scores were analyzed. Baseline characteristics and CYP2C19 genotype distributions showed no significant differences between groups (P > .05). Multivariate logistic regression revealed that the poor metaboliser phenotype significantly increased the risk of ischemic cerebrovascular disease odds ratio (OR) = 2.31, 95% confidence interval: 1.25-4.26, P = .008), alongside hypertension (OR = 1.87, P = .043) and diabetes mellitus (OR = 2.12, P = .024). Dyslipidaemia prevalence was marginally but not significantly higher across genotypes in the Mongolian group. After 3 months of treatment, the genotype-guided observation group exhibited significantly greater reductions in total cholesterol and low-density lipoprotein cholesterol, and a slight increase in high-density lipoprotein cholesterol (P < .05). Furthermore, the observation group demonstrated significantly superior neurological recovery National Institutes of Health Stroke Scale and improved daily functioning (ADL) compared to the control group (P < .001). CYP2C19 poor-metaboliser status is associated with an increased risk of ischemic cerebrovascular disease in the Mongolian population and may contribute to dyslipidaemia and treatment response heterogeneity. Individualised intervention guided by CYP2C19 genotyping offers potential benefits in improving lipid profiles, neurological function, and short-term outcomes, serving as a valuable tool for precision medicine in this population.","affiliation":"Department of Neurology, Tongliao People's Hospital, Tongliao, China.","publicationStatus":"ppublish","language":"eng","pubModel":"Print","pubTypeList":{"pubType":["research-article","Journal Article"]},"meshHeadingList":{"meshHeading":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Humans"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Cerebrovascular Disorders","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Brain Ischemia","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genetic Predisposition to Disease"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Risk Factors"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Case-Control Studies"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Genotype"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Polymorphism, Genetic"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Aged"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Middle Aged"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Mongolia","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EP","qualifierName":"epidemiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Female"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Male"},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Dyslipidemias","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"EP","qualifierName":"epidemiology"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"Y","descriptorName":"Cytochrome P-450 CYP2C19","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}},{"majorTopic_YN":"N","descriptorName":"Asian People","meshQualifierList":{"meshQualifier":[{"majorTopic_YN":"N","abbreviation":"GE","qualifierName":"genetics"}]}}]},"keywordList":{"keyword":["ischemic cerebrovascular disease","Dyslipidaemia","Mongolian Population","Cyp2c19 Gene Polymorphism"]},"chemicalList":{"chemical":[{"name":"CYP2C19 protein, human","registryNumber":"EC 1.14.14.1"},{"name":"Cytochrome P-450 CYP2C19","registryNumber":"EC 1.14.14.1"}]},"subsetList":{"subset":[{"code":"IM","name":"Index Medicus"}]},"fullTextUrlList":{"fullTextUrl":[{"availability":"Subscription required","availabilityCode":"S","documentStyle":"doi","site":"DOI","url":"https://doi.org/10.1097/MD.0000000000050807"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"html","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13632975"},{"availability":"Open access","availabilityCode":"OA","documentStyle":"pdf","site":"Europe_PMC","url":"https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC13632975?pdf=render"}]},"isOpenAccess":"Y","inEPMC":"Y","inPMC":"Y","citedByCount":0,"hasReferences":"Y","hasTextMinedTerms":"Y","hasDbCrossReferences":"N","hasPDF":"Y","hasBook":"N","hasSuppl":"N","hasLabsLinks":"N","hasData":"Y","license":"cc by","authMan":"N","epmcAuthMan":"N","nihAuthMan":"N","hasTMAccessionNumbers":"Y","tmAccessionTypeList":{"accessionType":["doi"]},"dateOfCompletion":"2026-10-02","dateOfCreation":"2026-10-02","dateOfRevision":"2026-10-05","firstPublicationDate":"2026-10-01","firstIndexDate":"2026-10-03","fullTextReceivedDate":"2026-10-05","hasEvaluations":"N"}]}}